#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/hardware/gpio-output/electronics-basics.rst:2
msgid "Electronics basics"
msgstr "电子学基础"

#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/hardware/gpio-output/electronics-basics.rst:4
msgid ""
"Driving anything external from a GPIO pin needs a circuit on the other side "
"of the pin. Three ideas from basic electronics -- voltage, current, and the "
"relationship between them through a resistor -- show up in every such "
"circuit."
msgstr ""
"要用 GPIO "
"引脚驱动任何外部器件，都需要在引脚的另一侧搭建一个电路。基础电子学中的三个概念——电压、电流，以及它们通过电阻建立的关系——会出现在每一个这样的电路中。"

#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/hardware/gpio-output/electronics-basics.rst:10
msgid "Voltage, current, resistance"
msgstr "电压、电流、电阻"

#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/hardware/gpio-output/electronics-basics.rst:12
msgid ""
"**Voltage** (volts, V) is the potential difference between two points in a "
"circuit. The chip's supply rail might be at 3.3 V relative to ground; a GPIO"
" pin driven high sits at the same 3.3 V."
msgstr "**电压**\\ （伏特，V）是电路中两点之间的电位差。芯片的供电轨相对于地可能为 3.3 V；被拉高的 GPIO 引脚同样处于 3.3 V。"

#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/hardware/gpio-output/electronics-basics.rst:16
msgid ""
"**Current** (amps, A, or milliamps, mA) is the flow of charge through a "
"wire. Current always returns to where it came from, so for any current to "
"flow, the circuit must form a complete loop from supply back to ground."
msgstr ""
"**电流**\\ （安培，A，或毫安，mA）是电荷通过导线的流动。电流总会回流到它的起点，因此要让任何电流流动，电路都必须从电源到地形成一个完整的回路。"

#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/hardware/gpio-output/electronics-basics.rst:20
msgid ""
"**Resistance** (ohms, Ω) is how much the path resists that flow. A "
"resistor's purpose is to set the current to a known value at a known "
"voltage."
msgstr "**电阻**\\ （欧姆，Ω）表示路径对这种流动的阻碍程度。电阻的作用是在已知电压下把电流设定为一个已知的值。"

#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/hardware/gpio-output/electronics-basics.rst:24
msgid "Ohm's law ties them together:"
msgstr "欧姆定律把它们联系在一起："

#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/hardware/gpio-output/electronics-basics.rst:26
msgid ""
"A triangle divided into three regions labelled V at\n"
"top, I and R at the bottom; the rearranged forms\n"
"V = IR, I = V/R, R = V/I appear around it."
msgstr ""
"一个被分为三个区域的三角形，顶部标记 V，\n"
"底部标记 I 和 R；其周围列出了变换后的形式\n"
"V = IR、I = V/R、R = V/I。"

#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/hardware/gpio-output/electronics-basics.rst:31
msgid "Ohm's law in its three forms."
msgstr "欧姆定律的三种形式。"

#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/hardware/gpio-output/electronics-basics.rst:33
msgid ""
"In words: the voltage across a resistor equals the current through it times "
"the resistance. Knowing any two of the three gives the third by algebra."
msgstr "用文字表述：电阻两端的电压等于流过它的电流乘以电阻。已知三者中的任意两个，便可通过代数运算求出第三个。"

#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/hardware/gpio-output/electronics-basics.rst:38
msgid "Diodes"
msgstr "二极管"

#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/hardware/gpio-output/electronics-basics.rst:40
msgid ""
"A diode is a two-terminal component that conducts current in one direction "
"(from *anode* to *cathode*) and blocks it in the other."
msgstr "二极管是一种双端器件，它只在一个方向（从\\ *阳极*\\ 到\\ *阴极*\\ ）导通电流，而在另一个方向阻断电流。"

#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/hardware/gpio-output/electronics-basics.rst:44
msgid ""
"A diode schematic symbol -- a triangle pointing right\n"
"into a vertical bar -- with anode marked on the left\n"
"and cathode on the right. An LED variant adds two\n"
"outward arrows next to the symbol indicating emitted\n"
"light."
msgstr ""
"一个二极管的电路符号——一个指向右侧、\n"
"顶在一条竖线上的三角形——左侧标记为阳极，\n"
"右侧标记为阴极。LED 变体在符号旁增加了两个\n"
"向外的箭头，表示发出的光。"

#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/hardware/gpio-output/electronics-basics.rst:51
msgid ""
"A diode conducts only from anode to cathode. An LED is a diode that emits "
"light while conducting."
msgstr "二极管只能从阳极向阴极导通。LED 是一种在导通时会发光的二极管。"

#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/hardware/gpio-output/electronics-basics.rst:54
msgid ""
"A diode also has a *forward voltage* (``Vf``) -- the voltage drop across it "
"when current flows in the conducting direction. Once the applied voltage "
"reaches ``Vf`` the diode behaves roughly like a wire; below it, almost no "
"current flows."
msgstr ""
"二极管还具有\\ *正向电压*\\ （\\ ``Vf``\\ ）——即电流沿导通方向流动时它两端的压降。一旦施加的电压达到 ``Vf``\\ "
"，二极管就大致表现得像一根导线；低于此值时，几乎没有电流流过。"

#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/hardware/gpio-output/electronics-basics.rst:60
msgid "LEDs"
msgstr "LED"

#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/hardware/gpio-output/electronics-basics.rst:62
msgid ""
"A *light-emitting diode* (LED) is a diode that converts its conduction "
"current into visible or infrared light. Brightness scales with the current; "
"colour is set by the LED's chemistry, not by the drive."
msgstr ""
"*发光二极管*\\ （LED）是一种把其导通电流转换为可见光或红外光的二极管。亮度随电流变化；颜色由 LED 的化学成分决定，而非由驱动方式决定。"

#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/hardware/gpio-output/electronics-basics.rst:67
msgid "Typical LED forward voltages:"
msgstr "典型的 LED 正向电压："

#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/hardware/gpio-output/electronics-basics.rst:69
msgid "Red: 1.8 -- 2.2 V"
msgstr "红色：1.8 -- 2.2 V"

#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/hardware/gpio-output/electronics-basics.rst:70
msgid "Green or yellow: 2.0 -- 2.4 V"
msgstr "绿色或黄色：2.0 -- 2.4 V"

#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/hardware/gpio-output/electronics-basics.rst:71
msgid "Blue or white: 2.8 -- 3.4 V"
msgstr "蓝色或白色：2.8 -- 3.4 V"

#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/hardware/gpio-output/electronics-basics.rst:73
msgid ""
"A useful operating current for an indicator LED is 5 -- 20 mA. Higher "
"currents are brighter but shorten the LED's life and may exceed the GPIO "
"pin's drive limit."
msgstr "指示用 LED 的合适工作电流为 5 -- 20 mA。电流越大越亮，但会缩短 LED 的寿命，并且可能超出 GPIO 引脚的驱动上限。"

#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/hardware/gpio-output/electronics-basics.rst:78
msgid "The current-limiting resistor"
msgstr "限流电阻"

#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/hardware/gpio-output/electronics-basics.rst:80
msgid ""
"Connecting an LED directly between a GPIO pin and ground would let almost "
"unlimited current flow: once the forward voltage is reached, the LED looks "
"like a near-short circuit. A *series resistor* between the pin and the LED "
"sets the current to a safe value."
msgstr ""
"把 LED 直接接在 GPIO 引脚与地之间，会让几乎不受限制的电流流过：一旦达到正向电压，LED 看起来就像一个近似短路。在引脚与 LED "
"之间串联一个\\ *串联电阻*\\ 可将电流设定到安全值。"

#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/hardware/gpio-output/electronics-basics.rst:86
msgid ""
"A circuit: GPIO pin connects through a resistor R to\n"
"the anode of an LED; the LED's cathode goes to\n"
"ground. Labels mark Vsupply at the pin, V_R across\n"
"the resistor, Vf across the LED, and the current If\n"
"flowing around the loop."
msgstr ""
"一个电路：GPIO 引脚经过电阻 R 连接到\n"
"LED 的阳极；LED 的阴极接地。标注显示引脚处的\n"
"Vsupply、电阻两端的 V_R、LED 两端的 Vf，\n"
"以及在回路中流动的电流 If。"

#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/hardware/gpio-output/electronics-basics.rst:93
msgid "A series resistor sets the LED current."
msgstr "串联电阻设定 LED 的电流。"

#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/hardware/gpio-output/electronics-basics.rst:95
msgid ""
"The supply voltage divides between the resistor and the LED: the LED drops "
"its forward voltage, the resistor drops the rest. By Ohm's law:"
msgstr "供电电压在电阻和 LED 之间进行分配：LED 上承担其正向电压，其余部分由电阻承担。根据欧姆定律："

#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/hardware/gpio-output/electronics-basics.rst:103
msgid "For a red LED (``Vf ≈ 2.0 V``) driven from a 3.3 V GPIO pin at 10 mA:"
msgstr "对于一个由 3.3 V GPIO 引脚以 10 mA 驱动的红色 LED（\\ ``Vf ≈ 2.0 V``\\ ）："

#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/hardware/gpio-output/electronics-basics.rst:110
msgid ""
"In practice, pick the nearest larger standard value (150 Ω or 220 Ω). The "
"result is a slightly dimmer LED with a healthier safety margin. Reach for "
"200 -- 470 Ω as a sensible default when exact brightness does not matter."
msgstr ""
"在实践中，应选取最接近的较大标准值（150 Ω 或 220 Ω）。结果是 LED 稍暗一些，但安全裕度更健康。当对精确亮度无要求时，200 -- 470"
" Ω 是一个合理的默认选择。"

#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/hardware/gpio-output/electronics-basics.rst:116
msgid "Why each piece matters"
msgstr "为什么每个部分都重要"

#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/hardware/gpio-output/electronics-basics.rst:118
msgid ""
"The shape of every GPIO output circuit comes out of the four ideas above:"
msgstr "每个 GPIO 输出电路的形态都源自上面的四个概念："

#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/hardware/gpio-output/electronics-basics.rst:121
msgid ""
"**Voltage** sets the energy available at the pin. A 3.3 V GPIO has 3.3 V to "
"spend across whatever is wired between it and ground."
msgstr "**电压**\\ 决定了引脚处可用的能量。一个 3.3 V 的 GPIO 拥有 3.3 V 的电压，可分配给接在它与地之间的任何器件。"

#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/hardware/gpio-output/electronics-basics.rst:124
msgid ""
"**A diode** (an LED, in this case) consumes part of that voltage as its "
"forward drop and refuses to conduct in the wrong direction -- it sets the "
"*which way* and the *fixed share*."
msgstr ""
"**二极管**\\ （本例中是 LED）以其正向压降的形式消耗掉一部分电压，并拒绝沿错误方向导通——它决定了\\ *导通方向*\\ 和\\ "
"*固定的分担份额*\\ 。"

#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/hardware/gpio-output/electronics-basics.rst:128
msgid ""
"**A current-limiting resistor** consumes the remaining voltage and turns the"
" leftover budget into a controlled *current*. Without it, the LED would draw"
" whatever current the pin can supply -- usually enough to destroy one or "
"both."
msgstr ""
"**限流电阻**\\ 消耗掉剩余的电压，把剩下的预算转化为受控的\\ *电流*\\ 。如果没有它，LED "
"会汲取引脚所能提供的全部电流——通常足以毁掉其中之一或两者。"

#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/hardware/gpio-output/electronics-basics.rst:132
msgid ""
"**Ohm's law** is what makes the resistor's value calculable: given the "
"leftover voltage and the desired current, ``R`` drops out by algebra."
msgstr "**欧姆定律**\\ 使得电阻的阻值可以计算：给定剩余电压和期望电流，\\ ``R`` 便可通过代数运算得出。"

#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/hardware/gpio-output/electronics-basics.rst:136
msgid ""
"Voltage, current, resistance, diodes, and one rearranged equation are enough"
" to design every basic GPIO output stage."
msgstr "电压、电流、电阻、二极管，再加上一个变换后的方程，就足以设计出所有基本的 GPIO 输出级电路。"

#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/hardware/gpio-output/electronics-basics.rst:139
msgid ""
"The same parts have been hiding behind the on-board LED all along. "
"``machine.LED(\"LED_RED\").on()`` lights the LED because the camera's board "
"already provides everything around it -- the current-limiting resistor, the "
"wire to ground, the LED itself -- and the class just toggles the silicon's "
"GPIO behind them. The \"one line lights an LED\" view is true; it is just a "
"short way of saying \"drive that circuit\". Strip the abstraction away and "
"exactly the circuit above is what remains."
msgstr ""
"这些相同的部件一直都隐藏在板载 LED 的背后。\\ ``machine.LED(\"LED_RED\").on()`` 之所以能点亮 "
"LED，是因为摄像头的电路板已经提供了它周围的一切——限流电阻、通往地的导线、LED 本身——而该类只是切换它们背后硅片的 GPIO。“一行代码点亮一个"
" LED”的说法是正确的；它只是“驱动那个电路”的简短说法而已。剥去这层抽象，剩下的正是上面那个电路。"

#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/hardware/gpio-output/electronics-basics.rst:148
msgid ""
":class:`machine.Pin` is the same silicon exposed without the surrounding "
"parts. The script controls the pin's voltage directly; you supply the "
"resistor (sized by Ohm's law), the LED, and the return path to ground. The "
"same four ideas come back, in slightly different combinations, behind switch"
" debouncing, PWM filtering, and motor drive."
msgstr ""
":class:`machine.Pin` 是同一块硅片，只是去掉了周围的部件后暴露出来。脚本直接控制引脚的电压；电阻（按欧姆定律取值）、LED "
"以及通往地的回流路径都由你来提供。这同样的四个概念会以略有不同的组合，重新出现在按键去抖、PWM 滤波和电机驱动的背后。"
